# Plugin repository

> This file marks this repo as a **plugin repository**. Read it, and then
> `INTEGRATION.md` beside it, before touching git here.

This repo is **two things at once**:

- a **skill-manager plugin** — `.claude-plugin/plugin.json` at the root,
  contained skills under `skills/<name>/`. Consumers install ONE unit at ONE
  version and address its skills as `<plugin>:<skill>`.
- an **integration repository** — `integration.toml` lists those same
  `skills/<name>/` directories as constituents. Each is a real repo with its own
  remote in a development checkout; the parent tracks their files as **ordinary
  blobs**, never submodules.

Managed by the `plugin-repository` skill, which is a specialization of
`git-integration-repo`. That unit owns the git model, `refresh.sh` and
`propagate.sh`, and `INTEGRATION.md` states its rules — all of which apply here
unchanged.

## Rules (in addition to INTEGRATION.md's)

1. **Constituents live at `skills/<name>/`.** That is where skill-manager and
   the harness plugin runtime look for contained skills. Add one with
   `<plugin-repository>/scripts/add-skill.sh`, never with the dependency's
   `add-constituent.sh`, which hardcodes `constituents/`.
2. **`plugin.json` and `skill-manager-plugin.toml` must agree** on `name` and
   `version`. Change them only with `scripts/release.sh`.
3. **Propagate before you refresh.** `refresh.sh` is `reset --hard` per
   constituent: any skill edit made in this parent, and not yet fanned out to
   the skill's own repo with `propagate.sh`, is destroyed by it with no diff to
   recover from.
4. **A skill edit published from an agent's home lands HERE, not in the skill's
   own repo** — the store copy of a plugin is a checkout of this repo. It is not
   finished until it has been propagated.

## The two directions

```bash
S="${SKILL_MANAGER_HOME:-$HOME/.skill-manager}/skills/git-integration-repo/scripts"
P="${SKILL_MANAGER_HOME:-$HOME/.skill-manager}/skills/plugin-repository/scripts"

# IN: pull every skill's upstream changes as ONE reviewable change
$S/refresh.sh && git add -A && git commit -m "pull skills to upstream tips"
$P/release.sh minor

# CHANGE: edit across skills in one worktree, one commit, one PR
skt ticket new TICKET-123     # worktree + its own Skill Manager home

# OUT: fan the merged change back to each skill's own repo
$S/propagate.sh TICKET-123 --push --mr

# CHECK: valid plugin AND valid integration repo
$P/verify.sh
```

## Manifest

`integration.toml` (constituents, host, compositions) and
`skill-manager-plugin.toml` + `.claude-plugin/plugin.json` (plugin identity and
shared deps). Scripts read all three. Keep them in sync when a skill joins or
leaves the bundle.
